  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n- A trough approaching the west coast will usher in a pattern\n  change this weekend. \n\n- The pattern over the next week will remain active with troughs\n  moving through the region. \n\nA closed low off the west coast is filling in and will become a\ntrough by the time it arrives in the northern Rockies Saturday\nmorning. A larger, stronger trough will remain off the US west\ncoast setting up southwesterly flow into the region. The southwest\nflow will cause warmer temperatures and rising snow levels, and\nwhile the trough will also bring some moisture, it won't be much.\nOver all, it will be a breezy, wet weekend, especially in the\nmountains as a result. \n\nSome cooler air will make it into the region by Monday, causing\nsnow levels to trend down slowly, but steadily. As the broader\narea of troughing migrates eastward, it will bring more cold air\nwith it, and snow levels will reach around 4,000ft late Tuesday or\nearly Wednesday. So some light snow showers could reach valley\nfloors in western Montana by mid or late next week.",
